figure out what to do next. The user is trying to rollback changes in their IT environment, specifically using Kubernetes and SRE tools. They've already used the get_previous_rollbackable_cmd tool, which returned an empty list, and then tried to use rollback_command, which also indicated no more actions to rollback. Now they need to decide the next step.\n\nFirst, I should check if there are any other tools available that can help. The available tools are wait_tool, rollback_command, get_previous_rollbackable_cmd, and r_submit_tool. Since the previous attempts to rollback didn't find any commands to undo, maybe the system is already in the initial state. \n\nThe user's goal is to rollback all changes until the system is back to its initial state. If there are no more commands to rollback, then the next logical step is to submit the result. The r_submit_tool is designed for this purpose. Using it would signal that the rollback process is complete. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they should wait for some time to ensure that all previous operations have been fully reversed. But since the rollback_command already indicated no more actions, waiting might not be necessary. Also, the wait_tool has a maximum of 120 seconds, but without a specific reason to wait, it's better to proceed to submit. \n\nTherefore, the correct tool to use here is r_submit_tool to finalize the task.\n</think>\n\nr_submit_tool\n\nSince there are no more rollbackable commands, the system has been reverted to its initial state. The r_submit_tool is used to formally submit the completion of the rollback process and finalize the task.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=334, prompt_tokens=911, total_tokens=1245, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--01