, changing the port from 9090 to 9091. The exact command would be:\n\n`kubectl apply -f - <<EOF\nspec:\n  template:\n    spec:\n      containers:\n        - name: sidecar\n          ports:\n            - containerPort: 9091\nEOF`\n\nBut the tool requires the command to start with "kubectl". So the correct command would be using `kubectl patch` or `kubectl apply` with the appropriate parameters. \n\nWait, the user might need to use `kubectl edit` to modify the deployment, but the tool\'s description says interactive commands are not supported. So `kubectl edit` is not allowed. Therefore, the best option is to use `kubectl patch` to apply the change without entering interactive mode. \n\nSo the final tool call would be a `kubectl patch` command that updates the sidecar container\'s port to 9091 in the user-service deployment. This should resolve the port conflict by ensuring the sidecar uses a different port than the main container.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl patch deployment user-service -p \'{\\"spec\\": {\\"template\\": {\\"spec\\": {\\"containers\\": [{\\"name\\": \\"sidecar\\", \\"ports\\": [{\\"containerPort\\": 9091}]}}]}}}\'"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b8777a7f885520ac', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 772, 'prompt_tokens': 4118, 'total_tokens': 4890, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd65-aeb3-7dd1-bba2-6b67fc9f5bc4-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl patch deployment user-service -p \'{"spec": {"template": {"spec": {"containers": [{"name": "sidecar", "ports": [{"containerPort": 9091}]}}]}}}\''}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b8777a7f885520ac'