" namespace. The next step is to apply the correct patch to the deployment to reconfigure the sidecar container\'s port from `9090` to `9091`, resolving the port conflict. The `exec_kubectl_cmd_safely` tool will execute the patch command with the correct syntax to update the container\'s port configuration.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 790, 'prompt_tokens': 4074, 'total_tokens': 4864, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd65-f2ee-7bb1-bd85-a9049e32d0ef-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4074, 'output_tokens': 790, 'total_tokens': 4864}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='ffce23c0-2785-4304-9e48-9ab855faf6f1'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to fix a port conflict in the user-service pod. The main issue is that both the main container and the sidecar are using port 9090, causing the sidecar to crash. \n\nFirst, they checked the deployments and found that the correct deployment name is "user-service" in the "social-network" namespace. Now, they need to update the sidecar container\'s port. \n\nThe previous attempt to patch the deployment failed because the command was incorrect. The user tried using "kubectl patch deployment user-service -p \'{\\"spec\\": {\\"template\\": {\\"spec\\": {\\"containers\\": [{\\"name\\": \\"sidecar\\", \\"ports\\": [{\\"containerPort\\": 9091}]}}]}}}\'" but got a "NotFound" error. Wait, no, the error was actually from the dry-run, but after checking the deployments, the name was found. So maybe the initial command was correct, but perhaps the JSON structure was wrong.\n\nWait, the user then used "k